 R←Test_Select_016(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;list
⍝ Exercise "Select" with ranges like "3-6" entered by the user.
⍝ This needs a user; the parser is exercised by "Test_Select_015".
⍝ Ranges were introduced in 3.1.0
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 R←T._Failed

 :If batchFlag
     R←T._NoBatchTest ⋄ →0
 :EndIf

 list←'Item '∘,¨⍕¨⍳10

 ∆Info'Info: this test needs you: next enter "?", then "3 - 6" and "5-5" - both must be rejected - and finally "1,2 4-6"'
 →T.PassesIf 1 2 4 5 6≡('Select several:' 1)C.Select list
 →T.PassesIf C.YesOrNo'Did the help mention ranges like "3-6"?'

 0 ∆Info'Info: next enter "8-12" - must be rejected - and then "a~2-9"'
 →T.PassesIf 1 10≡('Select several:' 1)C.Select list

 0 ∆Info'Info: next enter "3-6"'
 →T.PassesIf 3 4 5 6≡('Select exactly four:'(4 4))C.Select list

 0 ∆Info'Info: next enter "?", then "3-4" - must be rejected - and then "3"'
 →T.PassesIf 3≡'Select one:'C.Select list
 →T.PassesIf~C.YesOrNo'Did the help mention ranges like "3-6"?'

 R←T._OK
⍝Done
